destroyed homes in a deserted village  close to the front line  families that used to live here left  when this war started almost eight years  ago  only their broken belongings remain  russian bank separatist positions are  just over the horizon  ukrainian army soldiers tell us their  shelter has been repeatedly targeted in  recent days  craters gouged out by separatist  artillery shells are just a few meters  away  27 year old byrne has been at this  dugout for three months the ukrainian  soldier says separatists are using  higher caliber weapons than before  they are targeting infantry in the  dugouts i stood at the entrance and  heard first incoming 10 meters away from  me they shelled along the road we walk  along perhaps tried to hit our  communication lines  the shelling is much more frequent and  concentrated recently  soldiers take us along a trench to their  observation post  this used to be a separatist trench says  this soldier  there are still anti-personnel mines so  be careful where you put your feet if  you don't want to lose one separatist  positions are under 50 meters in that  direction  most of the men here we speak to say  they have very little hope that a  peaceful solution  can be  we stopped to film when suddenly the  whistle of an incoming shell  you see the bushes there says this  soldier well 23 meters from there is a  separatist trench  between us is a minefield  the bunker is small and cramped  26 year old kippish which roughly  translates as chaos started fighting the  separatists  at the beginning of the conflict eight  years ago  i can't understand putin's politics it's  stupid to be afraid of something when  there's no threat i can't remember when  nato has ever been a threat to russia  not since the collapse of the soviet  union and ukraine independence more than  30 years ago  but that's not what russia's leader  thinks  vladimir putin's vision of the future  remains unclear  charles stratford al-jazeera eastern  ukraine
 

